## Parts as a sheet

Each row is one part, with its `id`. Copy the sheet into a spreadsheet, change it, and paste the whole sheet into **Parts from a sheet** before submitting. The changes are listed for you to save or reject before anything is saved. A row with an `id` changes that part; a row without one adds a part. A room is a `room`, `hallway` or `stairs`. Its `beside`, `above` and `open` lists name its neighbours, separated by semicolons. For a new room, leave all three blank to take the neighbours from its footprint. Every link gets an internal wall part, and an open one is marked open. Doors are added by hand. A cell left blank keeps its value. A `-` before a room in a list takes that link out. A line with only its kind and name removes that part, unless another part uses it.

